{"id":1386,"level":43,"name":"Мат однією фігурою (2)","group":"Типові матові конструкції","format":35,"description":"Are there many pieces on the board? Then you have to look closely.<br />What can the other player do to get out of check?<br />Can he move his king?<br />Or can he get out of check by capturing of blocking?<br />You have not won the game until your opponent has no way of escaping check.  <p>Look at the examples:<br />In <strong>example 1</strong> the white knight can check the king in two ways. But only one makes mate.<br />Moving the knight to the red square is not smart. It would check the king, but the pawn can still capture the knight.<br />What you should do is move the knight to the green square. Now, it is checkmate.<br />The king is completely trapped by his own pieces. He can&rsquo;t escape.<br />This type of mate is called the smothered mate.</p>  <p>In <strong>example 2</strong> the white queen can check the king from a few squares. To make mate White has to pay attention to the knight. With the white queen on one of the yellow squares, the king is not mated. Black&rsquo;s knight can still block the mate.<br />By moving the queen closer to the king, Black cannot interpose. The queen should move to the green square: checkmate!<br /><br /><strong>What do you have to do?</strong><br />Checkmate the king with one piece. Be sure to pick the right square to give check.</p>","assignment":"","stickerID":22,"examples":[{"fen":"6rk/6pp/8/4N3/8/8/8/6K1 w - - 0 1","pgn":"{[%csl Gf7,Rg6][%cal Gh7g6]} 1. Nf7# *","text":"","format":35},{"fen":"6rk/6n1/6p1/8/5Q2/8/8/6K1 w - - 0 1","pgn":"{[%csl Yh2,Yh4,Gh6][%cal Gf4h4,Gf4h6,Gf4h2,Gg7h5]} 1. Qh6# *","text":"","format":35}],"puzzles":[{"id":56645,"fen":"6bk/6pr/8/4N3/8/8/8/6K1 w - - 0 1","pgn":"{Q=1} 1. Ng6# (1. Nf7+? Bxf7) *","format":35,"texts":["Чорний король задихається!"],"text":"","isMulti":0,"multiThemes":[]},{"id":57472,"fen":"3rkb2/3nrp2/8/8/4N3/8/8/6K1 w - - 0 1","pgn":"{Q=1} 1. Nd6# (1. Nf6+? Nxf6